secubox-metablogizer (1.6.0-1~bookworm1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Mosaic tab site-list cache (#974): GET /sites and GET /status used to
    recompute the whole fleet on every request (git x2 + du per site,
    ~14.6s measured for 172 sites on the board under load, blocking the
    module's single-worker event loop and observed hanging past 90s under
    concurrent traffic). New api/sites_scan.py + metablog-audit.timer
    (5 minutes) move that scan out of band, with an atomic same-directory
    tmp+rename write; GET /sites now only reads the cache and reports
    `available: false` explicitly when it hasn't been written yet or is
    unreadable, instead of returning an empty list indistinguishable from a
    genuinely empty fleet. POST /sites/refresh triggers an out-of-band
    rescan on demand (fire-and-forget, never inline). Mosaic + Sites tabs
    surface cache freshness/unavailability instead of silently showing
    stale or blank data.

